%I A400455 #28 Nov 08 2026 21:57:52
%S A400455 0,3,43,426,3764,28292,198028,1267310,7655112,43595307,236889734,
%T A400455 1230871766,6154715860,29686121315,138638775009,628291316644,
%U A400455 2769933893114,11901455543272,49928794133006,204815843021374,822718057371761,3239943262031511,12523079692903912
%N A400455 Number of 3-dimensional vector partitions of (n, n, n) in which every part has at least one zero coordinate and at least one part has exactly two nonzero coordinates.
%C A400455 The total number of unrestricted 3-dimensional vector partitions A219678(n) can be split into three disjoint sets based on the maximum number of nonzero coordinates among their parts. A000041(n)^3 counts partitions made solely of 1-dimensional axis vectors. The sequence a(n) counts partitions where parts have at most two nonzero coordinates, and at least one part has exactly two nonzero coordinates. Finally, A399611(n) counts partitions containing at least one part with three nonzero coordinates.
%C A400455 Thus, A219678(n) = A000041(n)^3 + a(n) + A399611(n).
%C A400455 For 1 <= n <= 4, we have a(n) > A399611(n), while for 5 <= n <= 22, a(n) < A399611(n). This crossover marks the point where partitions containing 3-nonzero-coordinate parts become more numerous than those strictly restricted to parts with at most 2 nonzero coordinates.
%D A400455 Richard P. Stanley, "Decompositions of rational convex polyhedra", Annals of Discrete Mathematics, 6 (1980), 333-342.
%H A400455 Jishnu Babu Ranitha, <a href="/A400455/a400455.txt">Python program for lista(n)</a>
%F A400455 a(n) = A219678(n) - A000041(n)^3 - A399611(n).
%F A400455 a(n) = [x^n y^n z^n] exp( Sum_{m>=1} (1/m) * ( 1/((1-x^m)*(1-y^m)) + 1/((1-y^m)*(1-z^m)) + 1/((1-z^m)*(1-x^m)) - 1/(1-x^m) - 1/(1-y^m) - 1/(1-z^m) ) ) - A000041(n)^3.
%F A400455 (The inner sum represents exact inclusion-exclusion over the 2-dimensional boundary faces and 1-dimensional axes of the positive orthant).
%e A400455 a(0) = 0: the empty partition has no mixed parts.
%e A400455 a(1) = 3: Total partitions A219727(1, 3) = 5. Pure axis partitions = 1^3 = 1. Partitions containing a part of support size 3 (A399611(1)) = 1. Thus a(1) = 5 - 1 - 1 = 3.
%e A400455 a(2) = 43: Total partitions A219727(2, 3) = 66. Pure axis partitions = 2^3 = 8. Partitions containing a part of support size 3 (A399611(2)) = 15. Thus a(2) = 66 - 8 - 15 = 43.
%t A400455 max = 22;
%t A400455 (*Construct the logarithmic generating function inside out*)
%t A400455 se = Series[
%t A400455    Sum[(1/m)*(1/((1 - x^m)*(1 - y^m)) + 1/((1 - y^m)*(1 - z^m)) +
%t A400455        1/((1 - z^m)*(1 - x^m)) - 1/(1 - x^m) - 1/(1 - y^m) -
%t A400455        1/(1 - z^m)), {m, 1, max}], {x, 0, max}, {y, 0, max}, {z, 0,
%t A400455     max}];
%t A400455 coes = CoefficientList[Exp[se], {x, y, z}];
%t A400455 a[n_] := coes[[n + 1, n + 1, n + 1]] - PartitionsP[n]^3;
%t A400455 Table[a[n], {n, 0, max}]
%Y A400455 Cf. A000041, A219678 (unrestricted 3D vector partitions), A219727, A399611.
%K A400455 nonn,new
%O A400455 0,2
%A A400455 _Jishnu Babu Ranitha_, Oct 25 2026
